<article class="env-lemma" id="0ABZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0ABZ">Lemma <span data-tag="0ABZ">68.17.7</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$, $g : Z \to Y$ be morphisms of algebraic spaces over $S$. If $X$ and $Z$ are decent (resp. reasonable, resp. have property $(\beta )$ of Lemma <a href="/tag/03JX" data-tag="03JX">68.5.1</a>), then so does $X \times _ Y Z$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Namely, by Lemma <a href="/tag/0ABX" data-tag="0ABX">68.17.3</a> the morphism $X \to Y$ has the property. Then the base change $X \times _ Y Z \to Z$ has the property by Lemma <a href="/tag/03L0" data-tag="03L0">68.17.4</a>. And finally this implies $X \times _ Y Z$ has the property by Lemma <a href="/tag/0ABY" data-tag="0ABY">68.17.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>